{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKE92EcZ1kRSpMvZCpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's expected. Vitest, like Vite, only looks for `vitest.config.*` or `vite.config.*` in the directory you run it from (its root). It doesn't search parent directories, so running it inside `packages/foo` with no config there means it uses the defaults.\n\nYou can fix this in one of three ways:\n\n- **Point at the root config:** run `vitest --config ../../vitest.config.ts`.\n- **Add a config to the package:** create a small `packages/foo/vitest.config.ts` that imports the root config and extends it with `mergeConfig` from `vitest/config`.\n- **Run from the repo root:** define the packages with `test.projects` (called \"workspace\" in older versions) in the root config, then run `vitest --project foo` from the root."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5813,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5813},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b7ef95-a515-4198-8dd9-87abb1c23de6","uuid":"6acc1278-3ba0-40f5-a227-7c1d2e925fa0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:46:01.131Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKE8k7WvjjQRfBpBVWf"}
